{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1135408-dark-eras-fan-to-the-strongest-\u2013-arcadia-mountains-\u2013-changeling-mage-werewolf-2e","id":1135408,"title":"[Dark Eras fan] To the Strongest \u2013 Arcadia Mountains \u2013 Changeling+Mage+Werewolf 2E","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-08-30T05:53:38-07:00","id":1135408,"title":"[Dark Eras fan] To the Strongest \u2013 Arcadia Mountains \u2013 Changeling+Mage+Werewolf 2E","content":"I started to read book on werewolf myths across Europe\u2019s history ( <a href=\"http://www.bosz.com.pl/books/571/Wycie-w-ciemnosci-Wilki-i-wilkolaki-Europy-Bartlomiej-Grzegorz-Sala/z/\" target=\"_blank\">this one</a> ) and probable found interesting setting place in times of <i>To the Strongest </i>Dark Era. It\u2019s all about <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Arcadia_(ancient_region)\" target=\"_blank\">Arcadia Mountains</a> in Greece in times of Alexander the Great. Idea for this topic is to make few pages fan add-on to <i>To the Strongest</i> chapter as working setting for Storytellers and players to use in at least <b>Changeling</b>, <b>Mage</b> and <b>Werewolf</b> 2E games.<br /> <br /> Some few opening info about Arcadia region and ideas:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Arcadia is highland region, at the center of the Peloponnese. It encircled by various mountains and <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Arcadia_(ancient_region)#Arcadians\" target=\"_blank\">Arcadians</a> are treated as highlanders by most of Greece. They are one of most old of Greece population \u2013 said to hail from Achaeans, ethnic group to be assumed as progenitors of Greeks - with many superstitions, but rather peaceful lives.</li> <li>Local tribes make League of the Arcadians that oposed Spartan\u2019s conquest in 7th century BCE. They joined Athens in Delian League and during the Peloponnesian War Arcadia allied with Sparta and Corinth. King Philip II, father of Alexander, has subjugded the region to Macedonian Empire. In near future, they join sceond Achaean League in 280 BCE.</li> <li><b>Changeling + Mage:</b> Fearie is also known as Arcadia. It comes from the simple fact that Arcadians were famous as superstitious folk worshiping strange things and region was thought as very beautiful. Publius Vergilius Maro will describe in 1<sup>st</sup> century in BCE in his <i>Eclogues</i> Arcadia as idyllic \u2018realm of timelessness\u2019. Interesting could be pointing that both changelings and Acanthus takes their realms name from more superstitious part of it\u2019s legend.</li> <li><b>Werewolf:</b> Greece Arcadia was place of famous Myth about <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lycaon_(Arcadia)\" target=\"_blank\">king Lycaon</a> cursed to become wolf. It\u2019s probably the birth place of Lykon\u2019Ur from 2E corebook\u2019s <i>Field of Dogs</i> setting.</li> <li><b>Werewolf:</b> From this region are also famous tales of humans from <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Antaeus\" target=\"_blank\">Antaeus</a> family becoming wolves by crossing the river. I could see interesting Wolf-Blooded Tell from it that bearer change from Hishu to Urhan and back simply by being wet \u2013 or crossing the running water.</li> </ol>They are just opening thought \u2013 if you got yours, feel free to share, we may make it into minisetting in <i>To the Strongest</i> times. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 09-30-2017, 02:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpa